/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Pick a depth xu of the neutral axis.
   - SP 16 plots Pu/(fckbD) against Mu/(fckbD²) with one curve per value of p/fck (p is the steel percentage), for Fe250, Fe415 and Fe500, for d′/D = 0.05, 0.10, 0.15 and 0.20, and for bars on two faces or spread round four faces.
   - A corner column bends about both axes.
   - Mux, Muy are the factored moments about x and y (each at least Puemin); Mux1, Muy1 are the uniaxial moment capacities about x and y at the same Pu; αn = 1.0 when Pu/Puz ≤ 0.2, 2.0 when Pu/Puz ≥ 0.8, and linear in between: αn = 1 + (Pu/Puz −
   - A circular section with equally spaced bars is symmetric about every diameter, so moments about two axes combine into one: Mu = √(Mux² + Muy²), checked as uniaxial bending.
*/
